<title>USA: U.S. Aug durable goods orders fell 3.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Aug durable goods orders fell 3.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department seasonally adjusted data on durable goods orders, with percent changes from prior months.</p>
<p>    Percent changes:	Aug    July--Rev from    June</p>
<p>  New Orders		 -3.1     1.4     1.7	-0.2</p>
<p>  Transportation Equip.  -7.9    -1.6    -0.4	-1.3</p>
<p>  NonTransport.Equip.    -1.6     2.4     2.1	 0.2</p>
<p>  NonDefense Orders	-3.5     3.5     3.6	-1.2</p>
<p>  Defense Cap Orders	9.0   -40.9   -36.7	26.4</p>
<p>  NonDefense Cap Orders -10.1     7.2     7.6	-4.6</p>
<p>  -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts   -5.0     3.9     4.2	 2.6</p>
<p>    Billions of dollars:  August    July---Rev from    June</p>
<p> New Orders		167.01   172.40   172.93    169.99</p>
<p> Transportation Equip.  37.87    41.10    41.59     41.76</p>
<p> NonTransport.Equip.   129.14   131.30   130.86    128.24</p>
<p> NonDefense Orders     161.79   167.61   167.79    161.89</p>
<p> Defense Cap Orders	5.22     4.79     5.14	8.11</p>
<p> NonDefense Cap Orders  41.37    46.01    46.18     42.92</p>
<p> -- Ex-Aircraft/Parts   36.90    38.84    38.94     37.39</p>
<p>Pct changes from prior months:</p>
<p>    -			   Aug    July--Rev from    June</p>
<p> Total Shipments	    0.3     0.5     0.8	-0.3</p>
<p> Total Unfilled Orders   -0.3     1.0     1.0	 0.7</p>
<p>In billions of dollars:</p>
<p> Total Shipments	 168.24   167.70  168.18    166.90</p>
<p> Ttl Unfilled Orders   478.87   480.10  480.15    475.40</p>
<p>New Orders--Pct changes from prior months:</p>
<p>    -			   Aug    July--Rev from    June</p>
<p> Primary Metals	    -2.7     1.6     1.0	-0.2</p>
<p> Industrial Machinery    -0.7     3.0     2.9	 0.3</p>
<p> Electrical Machinery    -5.6     4.9     4.7	 3.8</p>
<p>New Orders, in billions of dollars:</p>
<p> Primary Metals	   15.38    15.81   15.71     15.55</p>
<p> Industrial Machinery   32.41    32.63   32.61     31.69</p>
<p> Electrical Machinery   26.51    28.08   28.02     26.77</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had expected August durable goods orders to fall 0.1 percent. Excluding defense orders, they expected a 0.7 percent drop.</p>
<p>The 3.1 percent August drop in durable goods orders was the largest decrease since a 3.4 percent decline in April 1995, the department said.</p>
<p>It said the drop in August orders excluding defense was the largest decline since a 3.6 percent decrease in July 1993.</p>
<p>Orders excluding transportation in August had their first decline since March, while transportation equipment orders fell for the third straight month, the department said.</p>
